      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>The counting-song, “Eḥad Mi Yode’ah” appears for the first time in the Prague Haggadah (1526) in Hebrew and Yiddish, and was transcribed and translated into English by Aharon Varady. We are grateful to Isaac Gantwerk Mayer for proofreading and correcting the Yiddish transcription.</tei:p>
